# Cowgirl, Workshop, Slopes, And Chests

Consult `README.md` (Core gameplay, Campaign Workshop, Floor height, UI / art style, Agent rules 11–15). These are common regression areas.

## Cowgirl player art

- On-foot cowgirl sprites in `assets/player/cowgirl/` are **original handcrafted art** from `tools/handcrafted_cowgirl.py`.
- **Never** rebuild on-foot cowgirl frames by editing or copying cowboy sprites.
- Mounted rider art is separate: `tools/generate_cowgirl_horse_art.py` + `tools/cowgirl_hair.py` on `assets/world/cowgirl_horse_*.png`.
- Cowboy and cowgirl share animation names and frame counts; idle animation uses **one frame** only (no flickering idle_0/idle_1 alternation).

## Campaign Workshop

- Stamp hover ghosts and preview icons must show **final in-game size** via `CustomLevelStore.stamp_visual_world_rect`.
- **Right-click** removes a stamp on the grid or live preview.
- Stamp grid collapse uses a **▼ / ▶ chevron** (session state: `GameManager.workshop_grid_collapsed`).
- Do not regress to text-only hide/show labels or grid-cell-sized placement ghosts.

## Dune slopes

- Under curved desert banks, earth fill must stay dense in the upper wedge (no tile gaps exposing black/sky).
- Keep the warm `FloorSlopeUnderfill` wedge; do not leave featureless voids under the crust.

## Treasure chests

- Gameplay collision height targets **~109% of player height** (`TreasureChest.HEIGHT_RATIO`).
- Do not shrink chests back to old ~95% scale without updating README and tests.
